// THE MARKETS PROJECT'S OWN ELEMENTS (docs/TS_DECISIONS_2026_11_07.md §4, 2026-11-07, the user: "Add macro class
// obviously!"): beside the trading model (//scripts/corpus:trading_model, generated) and its Data (markets-data.pure,
// generated), the macro series the timeseries gallery reads -- a class of its own, its table, its mapping -- and one
// mapping and runtime for every class the gallery's and the markets page's copies over classes read
// (src/examples/on-classes.ts): the trading model's, through its stress::AllMapping, and this one.

###Pure
Class markets::MacroObservation
{
  series: String[1];
  date: StrictDate[1];
  value: Float[1];
}

###Relational
Database markets::DB
(
  Table MACRO_SERIES (SERIES VARCHAR(40) PRIMARY KEY, OBS_DATE DATE PRIMARY KEY, VALUE DOUBLE)
)

###Mapping
Mapping markets::Mapping
(
  include stress::AllMapping

  markets::MacroObservation: Relational
  {
    ~primaryKey ( [markets::DB]MACRO_SERIES.SERIES, [markets::DB]MACRO_SERIES.OBS_DATE )
    ~mainTable [markets::DB]MACRO_SERIES
    series: [markets::DB]MACRO_SERIES.SERIES,
    date: [markets::DB]MACRO_SERIES.OBS_DATE,
    value: [markets::DB]MACRO_SERIES.VALUE
  }
)

###Runtime
Runtime markets::RT
{
  mappings:
  [
    markets::Mapping
  ];
  connections:
  [
    // both stores through the project's one connection: a tile reading the prices and the macro series together is one
    // query on one session (lite plans a query on one connection)
    store::DB: [ environment: store::Conn ],
    markets::DB: [ environment: store::Conn ]
  ];
}
